==== JTAG ====
-> [[docs:techref:hardware:port.jtag]] general information about the JTAG port, JTAG cable, etc.

The port next to the flash chip on the top of the board is probably a JTAG header. The only known pin on the header is currently Pin 6 which is RESET.

===== Bootloader mods =====
-> [[docs:techref:bootloader]]

It is possible to flash u-boot on this device. Source code available here [[https://github.com/TobleMiner/u-boot-ralink/tree/master/MikroTik-RBM33G|U-boot rbm33g]]. However flashing U-boot on this device is neither required nor recommended since it won't work without modifying OpenWrt. It is recommended to just stick with the factory RouterBOOT.


